**Implementation Overview**

The implementation will consist of the following components:

1. FastAPI Application: This will be the core application that handles incoming requests and responses.
2. NGINX Reverse Proxy: This will be used to route incoming requests to the FastAPI application, with support for SSL termination and HTTP/2.
3. AWS EC2 Instances: These will be the cluster of instances that will run the FastAPI application and NGINX.
4. AWS ELB: This will be used to distribute incoming traffic across the EC2 instances.
5. Autoscaling: This will be enabled on the EC2 instances to automatically scale up or down based on the average CPU utilization.

