**Overview**

This project will design and implement a full-stack web application using FastAPI, with a load balancer and autoscaling capabilities, deployed on a Kubernetes cluster and served through NGINX. The application will have the following features:

* A simple RESTful API with endpoints for creating, reading, updating, and deleting (CRUD) items from a database.
* The API will be secured with OAuth2 and JWT authentication.
* The application will be containerized using Docker and deployed on a Kubernetes cluster with a horizontal pod autoscaler.
* NGINX will be used as an ingress controller to route traffic to the application pods.
* Load balancing will be implemented using Kubernetes' built-in load balancing capabilities and NGINX's load balancing features.
* The application will be monitored using Prometheus and Grafana, with alerts and notifications set up for when the application's resources exceed certain thresholds.
* A CI/CD pipeline will be implemented using GitHub Actions to automate the build, test, and deployment of the application.

**Architecture**

The architecture of this project will consist of the following components:

* **FastAPI Application**: This will be the core of the application, responsible for handling HTTP requests and interacting with the database.
* **OAuth2 and JWT Authentication**: This will be used to secure the API and ensure that only authorized users can access the application.
* **Database**: This will be responsible for storing and retrieving data for the application.
* **Docker**: This will be used to containerize the application and its dependencies.
* **Kubernetes**: This will be used to deploy the application and its dependencies on a cluster of nodes.
* **NGINX**: This will be used as an ingress controller to route traffic to the application pods.
* **Prometheus**: This will be used to monitor the application's resources and set up alerts and notifications.
* **Grafana**: This will be used to visualize the data collected by Prometheus.
* **GitHub Actions**: This will be used to automate the build, test, and deployment of the application.

